<title>GERMANY: DTB opens clearing system to non-DTB DAX options.</title>
<headline>DTB opens clearing system to non-DTB DAX options.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Frankfurt's Deutsche Terminboerse (DTB) derivatives exchange said on Tuesday that its members were now able to use the DTB clearing system for non-DTB options contracts on the DAX stock index.</p>
<p>The DTB said the move, effective immediately, was possible because DAX options contracts on other exchanges were identical to those on the DTB exchange.</p>
<p>The DTB also said it had started a &quot;block trade facility&quot; allowing members to input large-volume over-the-counter (OTC) trades into clearing system.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
